    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="64" column="1" str="/*x * Curl_auth_create_gssapi_user_message()x *x * This is used to generate an already encoded GSSAPI (Kerberos V5) user tokenx * message ready for sending to the recipient.x *x * Parameters:x *x * data        [in]     - The session handle.x * userp       [in]     - The username.x * passwdp     [in]     - The user&apos;s password.x * service     [in]     - The service type such as http, smtp, pop or imap.x * host        [in[     - The hostname.x * mutual_auth [in]     - Flag specifying whether or not mutual authenticationx *                        is enabled.x * chlg        [in]     - Optional challenge message.x * krb5        [in/out] - The Kerberos 5 data struct being used and modified.x * out         [out]    - The result storage.x *x * Returns CURLE_OK on success.x */"/>
